                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1263-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_8.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Bidirectional" title="Bidirectional" ></span>Coles Electroacoustics 4104</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Bidirectional Ribbon Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The Coles 4104 &#8220;lip microphone&#8221; is a noise-cancelling ribbon primarily used for broadcasting from noisy environments such as sports events.</p><p>The 4104 was original built by STC for the BBC. STC outsourced their production to Coles in 1974.</p><p>The mic is designed to be used very close to the mouth. The metal bar extending past the capsule is to touch the upper lip, ensuring the ideal distance.</p><p>The mic also features steel mesh nose and mouth guards. Removable plastic hygienic covers are included.</p><p>The 4104 uses a low-mass corrugated aluminum ribbon protected by fine woven nylon gauze. The ribbon is damped to control transient response.</p><blockquote><p><cite>Coles Electroacoustics</cite></p><ul><li>Better than 30 dB average discrimination between voice and background noise.</li><li>Provides speech of broadcast quality completely free from breath noises.</li><li>Flat frequency response at the controlled talking distance.</li></ul><p></p></blockquote><p>The 4104 is also available with a &#8220;Push To Talk&#8221; button (4104PTT).<p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Coles/4104">Coles Electroacoustics 4104</a> is also known as: 4104B, 4104PTT.</p>
